162
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:44,240
After all, their offensive play style does involve quite a lot of running approaches.

163
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:51,080
From an outsider's perspective, they may seem like they're doing a lot of unnecessary movement, but it's intentional.

164
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:55,280
Confusion is the key for them to pry open Shira Torizawa's defense.

165
00:10:55,280 --> 00:11:03,260
Tanaka, Asahi, and Daichi, who have been playing this whole time, must be beyond their body's limits by now.

166
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:05,360
Are you holding up okay, Nishinoya?

167
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:07,420
Yeah, just take your little breaks where I can.

168
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:12,520
Ushiwaka has scored close to 40 points, half of which he did single-handedly.

169
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:17,260
We've had him mark the entire game, and he's even had a lot of difficult sets.

170
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:20,360
I already knew it going into this game.

171
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:24,280
But Wakatoshi Ushijima is a beast.

172
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:26,440
Hey, Ushiwaka.

173
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:26,900
Hmm?

174
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:30,460
When you told me to pass to you, no matter what the situation was,

175
00:11:30,820 --> 00:11:33,260
you meant that like what you were still used for, right?

176
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:35,080
I'm just guessing here.

177
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:37,620
Hey, where did that come from?

178
00:11:37,700 --> 00:11:39,660
You can't just talk to someone like they're a little kid.

179
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:41,400
