199
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:05,180
Sorry!

200
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:06,160
All good!

201
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:09,400
My throw was fine, but my jump was off.

202
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:10,780
Great.

203
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,220
It looks like...

204
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:14,340
It's Ushiwaka's serve again.

205
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:31,140
That's on me.

206
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:31,960
It's all good.

207
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:35,400
When we get back, he's doing 100 serves.

208
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:38,460
Both sides are going for a risky approach.

209
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:41,720
That's pretty good for us, but it seems kind of wasteful.

210
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:43,980
I mean, it's all pointless if you miss, isn't it?

211
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:45,640
You're overlooking one detail.

212
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:48,500
A powerful serve can be a great intimidation tactic.

213
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:48,880
Yeah?

214
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:51,860
Now, a jump serve is a high-risk play.

215
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:56,040
However, it's not a simple choice between taking a chance or playing it safe.

216
00:13:56,040 --> 00:14:00,160
A team that's able to play more aggressively is going to be the stronger team.

217
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:06,160
A team that can choose to commit to a high-risk but big payoff play style will naturally thrive.

218
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:11,600
Of course, you don't want to be the team to blow it, but it's also a nice free pass when the other team screws up.

219
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:18,280
Which is exactly why there is a lot of value in acting like you've got nothing to lose.

220
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:27,020
It's yours!

221
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:28,860
Don't get baited.

222
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:29,780
Don't get baited!

223
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:30,620
Bait!

224
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:31,200
Hujuwaka!

225
00:14:41,780 --> 00:14:43,440
He's holding perfect form.

226
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:51,380
That was more about timing than it was height.

227
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:54,040
We jumped the gun a little too early on our block.

228
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:58,820
I know that everyone is exhausted and on edge, but think about this.

229
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:04,200
